% ============================================================================
% separation-methods.query.adj — a worked recall over the chemistry
% separation-methods library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how do you separate this
% mixture, and on what basis?": it states no chemistry fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `separation_basis` rows and returns the basis + the
% table's source/locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD
% (bind the basis `by_particle_size`, recall its method — filtration). A word
% that is not one of these separation methods abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a basis.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli separation-methods.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "separation-methods.adj"

? separation_basis(filtration, $Basis)        % expect by_particle_size
? separation_basis(distillation, $Basis)      % expect by_volatility
? separation_basis(chromatography, $Basis)    % expect by_different_rates
? separation_basis($Method, by_particle_size) % reverse bind — expect filtration
? separation_basis(centrifugation, $Basis)    % expect abstain — centrifugation is not one of the methods this source lists
